    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a78826752f2e2840152f6563b9f01df&id=8a7887a8a0abfc8001a0b01ecf8873c3": {
      "title": "Waukegan Campus BSN Program Curriculum Consultant",
      "description": "Dominican University Careers Careers JOIN OUR TEAM Position: Waukegan Campus BSN Program Curriculum Consultant Location: Chicago, IL Job Id: 2401 # of Openings: 1 Dominican University Waukegan Campus BSN Program Curriculum Consultant Position Type: This is an independent contractor appointment. Project Scope The Consultant will support the Dominican University Waukegan Campus through the program curriculum and operational development process to ensure a successful accreditation and regulatory approval application for the Waukegan BSN program.  Responsibilities include: Curriculum Content Development Develop a place-based, community-centered BSN curriculum for Dominican University’s Waukegan Campus that meets all accreditation (CCNE) and state (IBHE and IDFPR) regulatory requirements. Map all BSN coursework to ensure learning outcomes meet all accreditation and regulatory requirements. Develop curriculum plans for didactic, clinical and simulation laboratory experiences. Develop all program assessment and continuous improvement plan to meet accreditation standards. Clinical Partnership Agreement Development Recruit and establish clinical placement agreements with Lake County hospitals, clinics, and community agencies to fulfill all curricular and programmatic requirements of an accredited BSN program, ensuring adequate clinical experiences across content specialties. Program Faculty and Staffing Development Plans Develop faculty and staff position descriptions, faculty orientation and professional development plans. Waukegan Campus Facilities and Resources Planning Identify and inventory all supplies, equipment and facility needs for the Waukegan Campus BSN program. Identify all library and research resources needed to support BSN curriculum. Deliverables and Proposed Timeline Due by November 1, 2026 Prepare Waukegan Campus BSN program schedule concept map Prepare curriculum plan of study for the Waukegan Campus BSN Identify viable Lake County clinical practice sites to fulfill clinical curriculum needs for the projected BSN enrollment (i.e., 30 students per cohort). Collaborate with DU staff to ensure completion of all sections of the Illinois Board of Higher Education new program region application Due by April 1, 2027 Prepare all Nursing required course syllabi, including all accreditation standards aligned learning outcomes Collaborate with DU staff to prepare CCNE and IDFPR program applications for the Waukegan Campus BSN program approval Prepare equipment, resource and supplies inventories to implement BSN coursework Prepare faculty position descriptions and plans for faculty orientation, training and development Compensation Consulting services will be compensated at a rate of $ 5,000 per semester  with an estimated time frame of 10 months. Compensation will be paid in monthly installments. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Dominican University | (708) 366-2490"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a78826752f2e2840152f6563b9f01df&id=8a78879e9f4435c7019f6257ddd75523": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Library & Information Science (Tenure track)",
      "description": "Dominican University Careers Careers JOIN OUR TEAM Position: Assistant Professor, Library & Information Science (Tenure track) Location: River Forest, IL Job Id: 2353 # of Openings: 1 Position Title: Assistant Professor, Library & Information Science (Tenure track) Department: School of Information Studies (SOIS) Reports To: Associate Dean for SOIS Location: On campus (River Forest, IL) Expected Start Date : January 4, 2027 Position Summary: The School of Information Studies (SOIS) seeks an Assistant tenure-track faculty member specializing in archives, cultural heritage preservation, and/or digital-cultural stewardship with a strong, critically insightful interdisciplinary focus. The successful candidate for this position will contribute to teaching, advising, scholarship, and service aligned with the University’s mission and commitment to equity, inclusion, and social justice, as well as collaborate with faculty inside and outside SOIS. Further expectations include developing innovative/transformative curricular courses/initiatives addressing both emerging job market demands as well as socio-cultural needs in areas such as archives/archival theory and museums, records management, areas of digital stewardship (i.e., digital asset management, digital curation, digital humanities), cultural informatics, and community-based initiatives. Applicants should demonstrate expertise (or potential competencies) in cross-disciplinary and transdisciplinary partnerships, engagement with organizations that can provide experiential learning opportunities for students, and a demonstrated commitment to equity and inclusion in teaching as well as research. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Teach graduate courses in Library and Information Science at the master’s and doctoral levels with a standard teaching load of 21 credit hours, which corresponds to seven courses during the academic year. Contribute to the development, implementation, and ongoing assessment of the MLIS and PhD programs. Advise and mentor graduate students, including PhD candidates engaged in dissertation work. Engage in scholarly activity appropriate for tenure and promotion, including research, publication, and/or grant activity related to Library and Information Science. Contribute to accreditation, assessment, and continuous improvement efforts within the School of Information Studies. Participate in service to the School of Information Studies, the University, and the profession through committee work, professional engagement, and community partnerships. Collaborate with faculty across academic units on interdisciplinary teaching, research, and grant initiatives. Support partnerships with libraries, archives, and community organizations. QUALIFICATIONS : All listed qualifications are required unless otherwise noted: Earned PhD in Library and Information Science or a PhD in a related field and at least one earned degree in Library and Information Science from an accredited institution. Doctoral candidates who are on ABD status with an anticipated graduation date of August 2026 or earlier will be considered. Demonstrated preparation to teach graduate-level courses. Demonstrated commitment to inclusive, culturally responsive, and equity-centered teaching practices Evidence of scholarly potential and service consistent with expectations for tenure-track faculty. Ability to collaborate effectively with faculty, students, and community partners. Preferred Qualifications Practical experience in a library, archive, or information organization. Experience teaching, advising, and mentoring in master’s and/or doctoral programs. Experience teaching online, hybrid, and in person. Experience with program development, accreditation, and assessment in professional preparation programs. Record of or potential for external grant activity. CLASSIFICATION NOTE Candidates with additional relevant experience and demonstrated competencies may be considered for appointment at the Associate rank Salary and FLSA Status FLSA Status: Exempt, full-time SALARY: $65,000 - $81,000 Benefits Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance Retirement plan with employer matching contributions Professional development opportunities Tuition remission for employees and their dependents Flexible spending accounts (FSA) Generous paid time off (PTO) Employment at Dominican University is contingent upon the successful com To Apply: Applicants must submit a (1) cover letter, (2) curriculum vitae, (3) statement of teaching philosophy, (4) a sample of intellectual contributions, (5) an equity and inclusion statement, and (6) the names and contact information of 3 references. The cover letter should address work and other opportunities they have had to interact and serve in high needs and diverse populations and other interactions with students. Finalists in the search process will be asked to provide official transcripts. The applications must be submitted online at https://jobs.dom.edu A review of applications will start immediately and will continue until the position is filled. About Dominican University Dominican University is a Catholic, comprehensive teaching university located in River Forest, just 10 miles west of downtown Chicago, with an additional campus in the Pilsen neighborhood of Chicago. Accredited by the Higher Learning Commission, Dominican University offers associate, baccalaureate, master’s, and doctoral degrees. It is highly regarded for its academic rigor, thoughtful accompaniment of students, intentional affordability, and values-based, relationship-centered learning environment. Dominican currently enrolls over 3,800 students, including 2,690 undergraduates and 1,114 graduate students. Sixty-eight percent (68%) of undergraduate students identify as Latinx, 5% as Black or African American, and 3% as Asian. Under-represented minority students comprise 77% of the undergraduate enrollment and 38% of the graduate enrollment. Over 90 percent of undergraduates receive some form of financial aid. Nearly half of all undergraduates are first-generation college students; over half are federal Pell Grant recipients, illustrating their families’ level of income; and 58% are eligible for low-income MAP grants from the State of Illinois. Recognized since 2011 as a Hispanic-Serving Institution (HSI) by the U.S. Department of Education, Dominican is committed to expanding and enhancing educational opportunities for Latinx students and all students from historically underrepresented groups. For more information, visit www.dom.edu . Expectations for all Dominican Employees: To support the University's mission of preparing students to pursue truth, give compassionate service, and participate in the creation of a more just and humane world, engage in university service work that promotes collaboration and community building. This includes participating in organizational initiatives, supporting campus events, contributing to community outreach, and fostering a diverse and inclusive environment through involvement in various staff-driven activities and groups. Institutional Statement Dominican University is committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive academic community. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds. Upon request, reasonable accommodations in the application process will be provided to individuals with disabilities. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Dominican University is an equal opportunity employer and encourages applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, protected veterans, and candidates from diverse backgrounds. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by law. If you need accommodations due to a disability, you may contact us at opc@dom.edu for assistance. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Dominican University | (708) 366-2490"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a78826752f2e2840152f6563b9f01df&id=8a78839fa0f425e701a121386d642629": {
      "title": "Associate Professor, School of Social Work",
      "description": "Dominican University Careers Careers JOIN OUR TEAM Position: Associate Professor, School of Social Work Location: River Forest, IL Job Id: 2411 # of Openings: 1 Dominican University seeks an Associate Professor -River Forest, IL. The Associate Professor is a renewable, full-time position in our Borra College of Health Sciences in the College of Applied Social Sciences. As a diverse Hispanic Serving Institution, we center access, belonging, and equity-minded perspectives. We are seeking an individual who can demonstrate effective engagement in an environment where colleagues and students come from many backgrounds and identities, as well as someone who can demonstrate commitment to equitable and inclusive teaching, research, and governance practices. We are particularly interested in appointing a faculty member (Associate Professor) with practice and/or research focus one of these areas: Military Social Work, Gerontology, School Social Work, or historically excluded/minoritized communities. Requires Ph.D. in Social Work or a related field or within a year from completing Ph.D.   Mus have experience in commitment to teaching excellence and development regarding inclusive, critical, active pedagogical approaches, and a commitment to working with first- generation, immigrant, and/or underrepresented/historically excluded students. Additional skills and experience preferred include publication experience, experience and/or interest in developing community-based collaborations, demonstrated experience teaching or creating, organizing and/or leading programs for minoritized student populations, mentorship experience with Latinx and Black students and training or experience in culturally responsive teaching. Salary: $70,000.00 annually. Please apply to: https://www.dom.edu/jobs Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Dominican University | (708) 366-2490"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a78826752f2e2840152f6563b9f01df&id=8a7887a8a0abfc8001a0d534a9f870ec": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant – Career Programs & Data",
      "description": "Dominican University Careers Careers JOIN OUR TEAM Position: Graduate Assistant – Career Programs & Data Location: River Forest, IL Job Id: 2405 # of Openings: 1 TITLE: Graduate Assistant – Career Programs & Data Department: Career Programs Office, Dominican University Pay: $16/hour Hours: 15 hours/week Position Summary The Career Programs Office seeks a detail-oriented Graduate Assistant to support career readiness assessment, data analysis, and reporting. The Graduate Assistant will work with data from career and vocation courses, student and alumni surveys, and career outcomes instruments to help the office evaluate student engagement, career readiness and development, program effectiveness, and post-graduation outcomes. Responsibilities Analyze, interpret, and report career and vocation survey data. Review and analyze career readiness and career outcomes data from students and alumni. Examine data related to career readiness competencies and program learning outcomes. Identify trends, patterns, and key findings across available data sources. Create reports, tables, charts, and other visualizations to communicate findings clearly. Assist with survey administration, data collection, data cleaning, and documentation. Maintain data dictionaries, variable documentation, and other records to support consistent and reproducible analysis. Help translate assessment findings into actionable insights that can inform curriculum, programming, and continuous improvement. Support assessment and special projects within the Career Programs Office. Maintain confidentiality of student and alumni information. Qualifications Current graduate student. Ability to work with, interpret, and communicate data. Strong attention to detail and organizational skills. Proficiency with Excel or Google Sheets. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively. Preferred Majors/Education: Graduate students pursuing an M.S. in Information Management, M.B.A., or M.A. in Educational Leadership, particularly students with coursework or experience in data analytics, assessment, research, program evaluation, or data visualization Preferred: Experience with survey data, research, assessment, basic statistical analysis, higher education, career development, Qualtrics, Tableau, Power BI, or similar tools. Professional Development This position provides hands-on experience in data analysis, career readiness and outcomes assessment, program evaluation, survey research, data visualization, and higher education career programming. The Graduate Assistant will gain experience translating data into meaningful findings that can support program improvement and institutional decision-making. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Dominican University | (708) 366-2490"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a78826752f2e2840152f6563b9f01df&id=8a7885a89d930819019d9c205f32716f": {
      "title": "Graduate Reference Assistant",
      "description": "Dominican University Careers Careers JOIN OUR TEAM Position: Graduate Reference Assistant Location: River Forest, IL Job Id: 2280 # of Openings: 0 DEPARTMENT: Library REPORTS TO: Access & Reference Services Librarian MAXIMUM HOURS PER WEEK: 20 ITEMS TO INCLUDE IN APPLICATION: Cover Letter, Resume, and Class Schedule HOURLY RATE: $15.25 EXPECTATIONS FOR ALL DOMINICAN EMPLOYEES: To support the University's mission of preparing students to pursue truth, to give compassionate service, and to participate in the creation of a more just and humane world. JOB COMPONENTS//PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Graduate Assistants (GAs) in the Access & Reference Services Unit at Dominican University’s Rebecca Crown Library (RCL) are an integral part of the successful functioning of the library. GAs are often the first individuals that RCL patrons will interact with and can play a critical part in helping the Dominican community navigate library collections, services, and spaces. In addition to the value GAs bring to the library, working at RCL provides students currently enrolled in the graduate program in Library and Information Science with work experience in an academic library environment. Training provided helps connect you with best practices in reference work. You can build contacts with library professionals with a variety of specializations and experience levels. Also, independent projects can help you further hone your library skills and potentially work in a capacity that fits your future professional goals. Primary duties include: Staffing the reference desk at RCL and providing reference services in person and through live chat, email, and over the telephone Assisting student workers at the circulation desk with basic access services functions, such as circulating physical materials to patrons and handling student study room reservations. Conducting research consultations as assigned Working on independent projects as assigned Participating in library wide activities, such as assisting with collection maintenance and promotional work BASIC COMPETENCIES: (Required knowledge, skills, abilities) Currently be enrolled in the graduate program in Library & Information Science in Dominican University’s School of Information Studies (SOIS) Ability to work on site Strong interpersonal communication skills Strong customer service skills Ability to work with diverse populations and be committed to contributing to an inclusive work environment Dependability and punctuality Self-motivation and ability to work independently Comfort with technology and ability to learn new digital tools Must be eligible for US employment Must be enrolled at least part-time as a degree seeking student in a Dominican University graduate program. PREFERRED EXPERIENCE: Completed LIS 702 Facilitating User Learning and Information Needs course. Previous experience working in a library Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Dominican University | (708) 366-2490"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a78826752f2e2840152f6563b9f01df&id=8a7885a8a0abfd5001a0c9c862c72a29": {
      "title": "Graduate Student Worker – DU BeInvolved Engagement, Operations & Family Academy",
      "description": "Dominican University Careers Careers JOIN OUR TEAM Position: Graduate Student Worker – DU BeInvolved Engagement, Operations & Family Academy Location: River Forest, IL Job Id: 2403 # of Openings: 1 JOB TITLE: Graduate Student Worker – DU BeInvolved Engagement, Operations & Family Academy DEPARTMENT: Division of Student Affairs PAY RATE: $15.25 - $17.00/hour REPORTS TO: Division of Student Affairs DATES: September 2026-May 2027 HOURS: 20 hours per week SUMMARY The Graduate Student Worker will support the implementation, promotion, and day-to-day operations of DU BeInvolved, Dominican University’s student engagement and involvement platform, as well as provide support for the Family Academy program. This position will help increase student and campus partner engagement with DU BeInvolved by supporting event management, student organization outreach, training, and the distribution of promotional materials and giveaways. The Graduate Student Worker will also assist with Family Academy by supporting session preparation, family communications and outreach, attendance tracking, program materials, and other administrative and engagement needs throughout the academic year. The ideal candidate is organized, detail-oriented, comfortable working with students, families, and campus partners, and interested in student and family engagement. Responsibilities Review and approve events and activities submitted through DU BeInvolved. Add and update events and activities in DU BeInvolved. Ensure event information is accurate, complete, and follow guidelines. Provide basic training and support to student organizations and staff on how to use DU BeInvolved. Respond to basic questions and provide resources or refer more complex questions to the appropriate staff member. Help develop creative ways to promote DU BeInvolved to students. Assist with Suitable marketing campaigns, tabling and student engagement initiatives. Help promote DU BeInvolved during Welcome Week, DU Fest and other campus events. Assist with identifying and ordering DU BeInvolved promotional items and giveaways. Maintain an inventory of giveaways and promotional materials. Coordinate the distribution of giveaways at campus events and student engagement activities. Collect and review DU BeInvolved engagement data, generate reports, and track engagement trends. Assist with planning and supporting Family Academy sessions, events, and activities. Help create engaging content for the Family Academy newsletter and other communications. Communicate with Family Academy members by email and assist with sending reminders and updates. Help welcome and engage families during Family Academy events and sessions. Collect and organize program information, including attendance and participation data. Assist with tracking family engagement and maintaining accurate program records. Help promote Family Academy events. Take on other projects that help strengthen the Family Academy experience for students and their families Assist with creating flyers, social media content, or other promotional materials for DU BeInvolved and Family Academy. Other Responsibilities Assist with Suitable-related projects and initiatives as assigned. Maintain confidentiality and follow university policies and procedures. Provided feedback and recommendations for improving DU BeInvolved processes and student engagement. Provide general support with Family Academy projects and activities. Assist with OSI events on campus as needed. QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree required Enrolled in a Dominican University graduate program Ability to work flexible hours, including some nights and weekends Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Dominican University | (708) 366-2490"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a78826752f2e2840152f6563b9f01df&id=8a78839ea06420ea01a0a6da67f34f51": {
      "title": "Market Research & Survey Canvasser (Student)",
      "description": "Dominican University Careers Careers JOIN OUR TEAM Position: Market Research & Survey Canvasser (Student) Location: Chicago, IL Job Id: 2397 # of Openings: 1 TITLE: Market Research & Survey Canvasser (Student) Location: Little Village, Chicago Pay: $17.05/hour Hours: 10–15 hours per week during the month of October We are seeking a bilingual (English/Spanish) Dominican University student to conduct in-person market research with small businesses in the Little Village neighborhood. The canvasser will go door-to-door, engage with small business owners, and invite them to complete a brief 20–25 question survey on an iPad . Qualifications: Current student at Dominican University Bilingual in English and Spanish Familiar with the Little Village neighborhood Comfortable walking door-to-door for several hours Friendly, confident, and able to engage professionally with small business owners Available to work 10–15 hours per week during October Basic technology proficiency, including use of an iPad or mobile device Reliable, punctual, and comfortable working independently Responsibilities: Visit small businesses throughout Little Village Introduce the research project and explain the survey Encourage business owners to participate Assist participants with completing the survey on an iPad when needed Accurately record survey participation and follow research protocols Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Dominican University | (708) 366-2490"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a78826752f2e2840152f6563b9f01df&id=8a78859e9e46f63e019e474731450c8f": {
      "title": "Social Media & Communications Student Worker",
      "description": "Dominican University Careers Careers JOIN OUR TEAM Position: Social Media & Communications Student Worker Location: Chicago, IL Job Id: 2308 # of Openings: 1 Position Title: Social Media & Communications Student Worker Department: Director of Student Experience / Admissions Position Type: Part-Time Student Worker (10 hours per week) Hourly Rate: $16.60 Overview: We are seeking a creative, reliable, and outgoing student to join our team as a Social Media & Communications Student Worker. This role combines digital storytelling with in-person engagement to share the authentic student experience, support campus events, and help prospective students feel connected to our vibrant college community. Key Responsibilities: Social Media & Digital Content Create engaging content (photos, videos, stories, reels, blogs) for official college social channels. Highlight student life, academics, campus events, and community engagement. Assist with planning and scheduling posts using a content calendar. Monitor social channels for trends, mentions, and engagement opportunities. Support live coverage for campus events, tours, or special programs. Stay informed on current social media trends and suggest innovative ways to enhance the college’s online presence. Communications Support Help create email campaigns, Teams announcements, social media posts, and flyers to increase awareness of student services, activities, and opportunities. Qualifications: Current full-time student in good academic standing. Strong communication, writing, and interpersonal skills. Comfortable on camera and confident speaking to groups. Familiarity with platforms like Instagram, TikTok, Facebook, and LinkedIn (experience preferred). Skills in photography, video editing, or graphic design are a plus. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Dominican University | (708) 366-2490"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a78826752f2e2840152f6563b9f01df&id=8a7887ac9efb876c019f4338627a4cce": {
      "title": "Campus Experience Ambassador (CEA)",
      "description": "Dominican University Careers Careers JOIN OUR TEAM Position: Campus Experience Ambassador (CEA) Location: River Forest, IL Job Id: 2346 # of Openings: 1 POSITION: Campus Experience Ambassador (CEA) DEPARTMENT: Office of Undergraduate Admission REPORTS TO: Campus Experience Interns and Managers HOURLY RATE: $15.00 POSITION AVAILABILITY: August 2026 - May 2027 POSITION DESCRIPTION: Campus Experience Ambassadors (CEAs) are dynamic students who blaze the trail for every visitor, shaping first impressions and creating meaningful connections that inspire future students to see themselves at Dominican University. As part of the Campus Experience Team, CEAs are at the heart of campus engagement. They lead high-impact campus tours, support admission events, welcome guests at the Welcome Center & Information Desks (WID), manage visitor communications, and connect the campus community with the people, places, and resources that define the Dominican experience. Every interaction is an opportunity to inform, inspire, and make someone feel at home. CEAs develop professional communication skills, confidence, and storytelling abilities while serving as a student voice of the University. Through authentic hospitality, energy, and pride in Dominican’s campus community, CEAs are at the forefront of creating a vibrant, welcoming, and positive experience for everyone! EXPECTATIONS FOR ALL DOMINICAN EMPLOYEES: To support the University's mission of preparing students to pursue truth, to give compassionate service, and to participate in the creation of a more just and humane world. JOB COMPONENTS//PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Lead engaging campus tours that provide prospective students and families with a welcoming, informative, and personalized experience. Represent Dominican University with enthusiasm and authenticity while showcasing campus life, academic opportunities, and the student experience. Support admission events, including open houses, admitted student days, receptions, student panels, and group visits, by delivering exceptional hospitality, professionalism, and relationship-centered customer service. Enhance the visitor experience by warmly greeting and assisting guests and the campus community at the Welcome Center and Information Desks (WID), providing clear campus navigation, and connecting visitors with campus departments, services, and resources to ensure a seamless and supportive experience. Foster an inclusive and welcoming environment where current students, prospective students, families, and guests feel valued, respected, and excited to engage with Dominican University through genuine conversation and exceptional service. Serve as a primary point of contact across phone, LiveChat, and email communications, providing accurate, timely information and connecting individuals with the appropriate campus resources and support services. Participate in required training sessions, team meetings, and ongoing professional development opportunities to strengthen skills, enhance performance, and support a consistently high-quality visitor experience. REQUIREMENTS AND ELIGIBILITY: Must be a currently enrolled Dominican University student with a minimum cumulative GPA of 2.50 Demonstrate strong communication, interpersonal, and leadership skills. Have a passion for Dominican University and a desire to share your student experience. Provide exceptional hospitality, customer service, and create welcoming experiences. Work effectively with diverse individuals and foster an inclusive environment. Demonstrate involvement on campus or within the community. Complete all required training for Campus Tours and Welcome Center & Information Desk (WID) locations. Must be available to attend and support the 6 large-scale Saturday Admission Events: Discover Dominican Open House (November & April) and Admitted Student Days (February, March & April). COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS: Being part of the Campus Experience Team is more than just an on-campus job, it’s an opportunity to: Build your resume and reference list; Enhance your professional development; Develop and/or improve your communication and leadership skills; Network and bond with administration, faculty, staff, and fellow peers. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Dominican University | (708) 366-2490"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a78826752f2e2840152f6563b9f01df&id=8a78879e9fd3ba5c01a015c36fcc49f4": {
      "title": "Chemical Stockroom Assistant",
      "description": "Dominican University Careers Careers JOIN OUR TEAM Position: Chemical Stockroom Assistant Location: River Forest, IL Job Id: 2379 # of Openings: 1 TITLE: Chemical Stockroom Assistant FLSA Status: Hourly REPORTS TO: Senior Lecturer OPEN TO: Undergraduate Students AVAILABLE: Fall 2026 HOURLY RATE: 15.00 Position Summary: The Student Chemical Stockroom Assistant supports the safe, organized, and efficient operation of the chemistry department’s chemical stockroom and related laboratory support areas. Under supervision, the student assists with chemical inventory, storage, labeling, safety documentation, stockroom organization, and preparation of materials for teaching laboratories. This position provides practical experience in laboratory operations, chemical safety, and regulatory compliance. Key Responsibilities: Maintaining chemical inventory records; receiving, identifying, labeling, dating, and properly storing chemicals and supplies; organizing storage according to compatibility and safety requirements; and monitoring stock levels, expiration dates, damaged containers, and missing labels. Required: 1 year of general chemistry Preferred: 1 year General Chemistry, 1 year Organic Chemistry Physical Requirements: Ability to stand for extended periods during laboratory sessions. Ability to wear required personal protective equipment, including a laboratory coat, safety goggles, and gloves. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Dominican University | (708) 366-2490"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a78826752f2e2840152f6563b9f01df&id=8a78859f9f44356c019f866458c63fe0": {
      "title": "Kids Klub Assistant Teacher",
      "description": "Dominican University Careers Careers JOIN OUR TEAM Position: Kids Klub Assistant Teacher Location: River Forest, IL Job Id: 2364 # of Openings: 1 TITLE: Kids Klub Assistant Teacher FLSA STATUS: Non-Exempt Hourly DEPARTMENT : St Giles Preschool, 1101 Columbian Ave., Oak Park, IL 60302 HOURLY RATE: $16.50 REPORTS TO: Kids Klub Supervisor and Director of Early Childhood HOURS NEEDED PER WEEK : Monday - Friday 7:00 - 9:00 am 2:00/3:00pm - 5:30/6:00pm Must be eligible for Federal Work Study PRIMARY PURPOSE/POSITION SUMMARY: To assist the classroom teacher in providing a warm, nurturing environment where children can grow physically, emotionally, and intellectually. EXPECTATIONS FOR ALL DOMINICAN EMPLOYEES: To support the University’s mission of preparing students to pursue truth, give compassionate service, and participate in creating a more just and humane world. JOB COMPONENTS/PRINCIPLE DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Help teachers maintain a productive learning environment in the classroom. Help teachers maintain cleanliness in the classroom. Know where the students are at all times. Supervise indoor and outdoor play. Read and interact with students to promote learning. Demonstrate ability to use independent judgment and initiative to support children in learning and safety. Performs other duties as requested. QUALIFICATIONS: Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Basic knowledge of child development Flexibility Must be at least 18 years of age Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Dominican University | (708) 366-2490"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a78826752f2e2840152f6563b9f01df&id=8a7885aca0abfc6901a0c47c066d48e6": {
      "title": "Office Services Mail Clerk",
      "description": "Dominican University Careers Careers JOIN OUR TEAM Position: Office Services Mail Clerk Location: River Forest, IL Job Id: 2402 # of Openings: 0 Position Title: Mail/Office Clerk Date job is available: Fall 2026 Number of Positions (of this title) Available: 2 Hours per week (per position): 10 Dates/times needed (open shifts): Monday-Friday 8 am - 6 pm List dates of employment: Fall 2026 and Spring 2027 Position is open to: Undergraduate students only Rate: 15.00/hour Office Services/ Mail Room Clerk Position Responsibilities: Receive, sort and deliver all mail and packages to the proper destinations. (Offices and Mailboxes, Priory Campus) Assist with copy, binding, scanning and other requests submitted to Office Services Meter all outgoing mail Assist customers at the Office Services window with all requests and questions they might have. Perform other duties as requested, delegated or assigned. Excellent communication and customer service skills Telephone etiquette skills Ability to problem solve and make decisions Ability to take direction and follow through on assigned tasks Basic computer and office skills Maintain a professional work environment and attitude Requirements Must be enrolled at least at part-time, degree-seeking student status at Dominican University. Must be eligible for US employment. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Dominican University | (708) 366-2490"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a78826752f2e2840152f6563b9f01df&id=8a78879ea0f4259701a10da01e185488": {
      "title": "Recording Studio Graduate Assistant",
